{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-06T11:15:21.827Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"846e95d7599b737e9f76326d","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-vcs-w3yi"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Disambiguate parent object-fetch endpoints from nested objects repositories"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The catalogue-first disposition for PR #91 makes tenant/objects reachable but intentionally gives the deeper repository precedence at the ambiguous path tenant/objects/fetch. Consequently a parent-scoped token cannot use that path for the tenant repository object-fetch endpoint while the nested repository exists. This is a residual wire-layout ambiguity, beyond the promised minimal catalogue-precedence fix; ordinary parent fetch and nested clone remain reachable."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-06T11:15:21.827Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-06T11:15:21.827Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex-sol"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"An explicit wire address or compatible negotiation makes parent fetchObjects and nested repository fetch reachable together; regression tests cover no-auth, parent-only, nested-only and multi-repository grants; unauthorized requests retain the fixed denial shape."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-vcs-ttc0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Serve repositories tenant and tenant/objects with distinct read grants. The catalogue-precedence regression in test/serve.test.ts asserts that the nested grant fetches successfully at tenant/objects/fetch and the parent grant receives the fixed denial there. HttpTransport.fetchObjects for the parent uses the same path."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Both repositories and every supported endpoint can be addressed unambiguously, including with a grant that reaches both repositories and without authentication."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The nested repository shadows the parent objects/fetch endpoint at their shared URL path."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/files","value":[{"path":"engine/http-transport.ts","scope":"project"},{"path":"engine/serve.ts","scope":"project"},{"path":"test/serve.test.ts","scope":"project"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/docs","value":[{"path":"README.md","scope":"project"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"3f9d27b8c931c753198b7641f47afea863da0012eead4075a53d1856a9e50753","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ac1f96bcc33733716e2310a020929695df04904ac2b2574ba2371fbafba602d3"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-06T23:09:24.225Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"1c3d835edba106c1302b3106","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.291","source":"probe"}},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Without --auth, or for a token scoped to both repositories, the nested repository shadows the parent's objects/fetch endpoint at their shared URL path. Parent-only tokens are not affected since 7341b0d."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Serve repositories tenant and tenant/objects (a) without --auth, or (b) with one token granted read on both. Request POST /tenant/objects/fetch: it resolves to repository tenant/objects, endpoint fetch. HttpTransport.fetchObjects for the parent uses the same path, so the parent's object fetch is shadowed."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-06T23:09:24.225Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Served paths resolve among the candidates the caller may read, deepest catalogued first (7341b0d). A token granted only the parent therefore reaches the parent's objects/fetch endpoint at tenant/objects/fetch, and the answer does not depend on whether tenant/objects exists. A residual wire-layout ambiguity remains in two cases: a server without --auth (every candidate is in scope), and a token granted both tenant and tenant/objects. In both, the nested repository takes precedence at tenant/objects/fetch, so the parent's object-fetch endpoint is unreachable at that URL while the nested repository exists."}],"before_hash":"3f9d27b8c931c753198b7641f47afea863da0012eead4075a53d1856a9e50753","after_hash":"8d51cd64fb14ba6cf3f5